Spectral libraries
------------------
Location:  tetracorder/sl1/usgs/library06.conv/  (splib06b, sprlb06b)
Source:    Copied from spectroscopy-tetracorder (see above).
           splib06 is the USGS Digital Spectral Library:
           Clark, R.N., et al., 2007, USGS digital spectral library splib06a:
           U.S. Geological Survey, Digital Data Series 231,
           https://doi.org/10.3133/ds231
           sprlb06 is the companion research library distributed with
           Tetracorder.


DaVinci
-------
Location:  not in this repository; the Containerfile installs it into the
           container image from ASU's prebuilt package
Upstream:  Arizona State University, Mars Space Flight Facility,
           https://davinci.asu.edu
Source:    https://oss.mars.asu.edu/svn/davinci/davinci/trunk
License:   GNU General Public License, version 2

Tetracorder's colour products and browse images are DaVinci scripts
(tetracorder/tetracorder.cmds/*/davinci-cmds.for.usr.local.bin/). They run as
programs interpreted by DaVinci and are not linked into it.


Container images
----------------
A container image built from this repository is an aggregate of separate
programs. Each program keeps its own license: tetrapy (Apache-2.0),
Tetracorder/specpr (GPL-3.0 with the PSI conditions), DaVinci (GPL-2.0), and
the Ubuntu, conda-forge and PyPI packages in the image (their own licenses).
The corresponding source for the GPL components is available at the upstream
locations above. The Tetracorder/specpr source is also in this repository at
the commit the image was built from.
